---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import MethodCaseStudies from '../components/MethodCaseStudies.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';

const homeHref = withBase('/');
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
const chapters = [
  { id: 'principles', label: 'Principles' },
  { id: 'think', label: 'Think' },
  { id: 'act', label: 'Act' },
  { id: 'respond', label: 'Respond' },
  { id: 'case-studies', label: 'Case studies' },
];
---

<Base
  title="How I Work | First Principles, Intuition, and Execution"
  description="How a Senior Engineer thinks through a challenge, acts on evidence, responds to setbacks, and carries a solution into production with case studies."
  canonicalPath="/method.html"
>
  <header class="method-header" id="top">
    <a class="method-wordmark" href={homeHref} aria-label="Return to portfolio">
      <span class="wordmark-mark">MK</span>
      <span>
        <strong>Mrityunjay Kumar</strong>
        <small>Applied science · ML systems</small>
      </span>
    </a>
    <a class="back-link" href={homeHref}>
      Portfolio <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={15} />
    </a>
  </header>

  <main id="main" class="method-page">
    <section class="method-hero" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">How I work</p>
        <h1 id="method-title">First principles make intuition executable.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">
          Understand the problem. Make a deliberate move. Learn from what happens.
          I try to make that loop explicit, from the first uncertain question to the
          system someone actually uses.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="#principles">Start with the principles <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
      </div>

      <aside class="position-note" aria-label="Working position">
        <p class="mono-label">Mrityunjay Kumar</p>
        <p class="role-note"><strong>Senior ML Engineer</strong> at Microsoft</p>
        <p>
          Intuition is compressed evidence. It helps me choose where to look;
          it does not excuse me from checking what I find.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <nav class="method-nav" aria-label="Method chapters">
      <ol>
        {chapters.map((chapter, index) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`#${chapter.id}`}>
              <span aria-hidden="true">0{index + 1}</span>{chapter.label}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <section id="principles" class="method-section principles" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / Principles</p>
        <h2 id="principles-title">Start with what must be true.</h2>
        <p>
          Tools change. These are the habits I return to when the problem is ambiguous,
          the system is unfamiliar, or an apparently good answer does not survive contact
          with reality.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="principle-list">
        <li>
          <h3>Separate facts from assumptions.</h3>
          <p>I want to know what was observed, what was inferred, and what is still unknown.
            Confidence is not a substitute for that distinction.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Explain the mechanism.</h3>
          <p>I work backward from the symptom to the state, dependencies, and constraints
            that could produce it. A fix should follow from an explanation.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Make uncertainty testable.</h3>
          <p>I prefer a small experiment that could prove me wrong to a large implementation
            that only makes the original assumption harder to revisit.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Own the outcome, not just the change.</h3>
          <p>The job includes checking what reaches the user, documenting the remaining
            limits, and leaving the next person a system they can reason about.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="think" class="method-section thinking-section" aria-labelledby="think-title">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / How I think</p>
        <h2 id="think-title">Frame the challenge before choosing the tool.</h2>
        <p>
          I first turn a broad request into a specific decision. The aim is not to model
          everything. It is to understand enough to choose the next useful question.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="question-grid">
        <article>
          <p class="mono-label">Outcome</p>
          <h3>What needs to become better, and for whom?</h3>
          <p>Identify the user, the failure they experience, and the observation that would
            distinguish an improvement from a merely different result.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="mono-label">System</p>
          <h3>What can change, and what must stay true?</h3>
          <p>Map the relevant inputs, state, dependencies, and constraints. Keep the failure
            boundary clear enough to tell a local problem from an upstream one.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="mono-label">Uncertainty</p>
          <h3>Which assumption would change the decision?</h3>
          <p>Write down a plausible explanation and a competing one. Choose the smallest
            observation that can tell them apart.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="decision-note">
        <strong>Before I implement:</strong> I should be able to name the outcome, the constraints,
        the working hypothesis, and the evidence that would change my mind.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="act" class="method-section action-section" aria-labelledby="act-title">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / How I act</p>
        <h2 id="act-title">Make one deliberate move. Close the loop.</h2>
        <p>
          Once the question is clear, I favor short, inspectable steps. Each step should
          either improve the system or reduce uncertainty about why it behaves as it does.
        </p>
        <p class="tool-note">
          <strong>Where AI fits.</strong> It can accelerate search, drafting, and implementation.
          I still own the question, the acceptance criteria, and the decision to ship.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="action-list" aria-label="From hypothesis to delivery">
        <li>
          <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <div><h3>Capture the starting point.</h3><p>Reproduce the behavior and record the
            baseline. Decide what will count as success before changing the system.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <div><h3>Make a focused change.</h3><p>Work on the smallest part that tests the
            hypothesis. Keep the change understandable and easy to revise or undo.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <div><h3>Check the result, then its neighbors.</h3><p>Run the focused check first.
            Then look for regressions, boundary cases, and consequences outside the local fix.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <div><h3>Verify delivery and leave a record.</h3><p>Check the built or deployed result,
            not only the source. Retain the test, decision, and known limits for the next change.</p></div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="respond" class="method-section response-section" aria-labelledby="respond-title">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">04 / How I respond</p>
        <h2 id="respond-title">When the evidence changes, change the plan.</h2>
        <p>
          A failed experiment is useful if it changes the next decision. I try not to defend
          an implementation or a research claim simply because I have invested in it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="response-grid">
        <article>
          <p class="mono-label">The test fails</p>
          <h3>Locate the broken assumption.</h3>
          <p>Separate an implementation defect from a faulty test, a bad measurement, or an
            incorrect model. Reduce the failure before broadening the fix.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="mono-label">The signals disagree</p>
          <h3>Investigate rather than average.</h3>
          <p>Check whether the measurements answer the same question. One reassuring score
            should not conceal a failure visible through another instrument.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="mono-label">The trade-off is real</p>
          <h3>Choose explicitly, and bound the claim.</h3>
          <p>Revisit the goal, cost, and constraints with the people affected. Narrow the scope,
            change direction, or stop, and explain what the evidence does and does not support.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="decision-note"><strong>The loop:</strong> understand → act → observe → revise.
        A solution is ready when it addresses the original need and its remaining risks are understood.</p>
    </section>

    <MethodCaseStudies />
  </main>

  <SiteFooter name="Mrityunjay Kumar" year={year} />
</Base>

<style>
  .method-header {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 20;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    min-height: 68px;
    padding: 0 var(--gutter);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--paper) 88%, transparent);
    backdrop-filter: blur(18px) saturate(1.25);
  }

  .method-wordmark,
  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .method-wordmark {
    gap: 11px;
  }

  .method-wordmark > span:last-child {
    display: grid;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .method-wordmark strong {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .method-wordmark small {
    margin-top: 3px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .wordmark-mark {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .back-link {
    gap: 7px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 550;
  }

  .method-hero,
  .method-section,
  .method-nav {
    padding-inline: var(--gutter);
  }

  .method-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 280px);
    gap: clamp(40px, 7vw, 96px);
    align-items: end;
    padding-block: clamp(64px, 7vw, 96px);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3 {
    font-family: var(--display);
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 16ch;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5.4vw, 76px);
    font-weight: 680;
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
  }

  .hero-lede {
    max-width: 54ch;
    margin-top: 28px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: clamp(18px, 1.4vw, 21px);
  }

  .text-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    min-height: 44px;
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
    text-underline-offset: 5px;
  }

  .position-note {
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }

  .position-note .mono-label {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .role-note {
    margin-block: 12px 20px;
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .position-note p:last-child {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .method-nav {
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--panel);
  }

  .method-nav ol {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    column-gap: 24px;
    list-style: none;
    padding-block: 12px;
  }

  .method-nav li {
    flex: 1 1 130px;
  }

  .method-nav a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    min-height: 44px;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .method-nav a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .method-nav a span {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .method-section {
    padding-block: clamp(64px, 7vw, 96px);
    scroll-margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .section-intro {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .section-intro h2 {
    max-width: 25ch;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 3.3vw, 44px);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .section-intro > p:not(.eyebrow) {
    margin-top: 22px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 17px;
  }

  .principles,
  .action-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr);
    gap: clamp(40px, 6vw, 88px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .principle-list,
  .action-list {
    list-style: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }

  .principle-list li,
  .action-list li {
    padding-block: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .principle-list p,
  .action-list p,
  .question-grid article > p:last-child,
  .response-grid article > p:last-child {
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .thinking-section {
    background: var(--panel);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .question-grid,
  .response-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 32px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .question-grid article,
  .response-grid article {
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  }

  .question-grid .mono-label,
  .response-grid .mono-label {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .decision-note {
    margin-top: 40px;
    padding-left: 20px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 86ch;
  }

  .decision-note strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .action-section {
    background: var(--ink-deep);
    color: #fff;
  }

  .action-section .eyebrow,
  .step-number {
    color: var(--accent-on-dark);
  }

  .action-section .section-intro > p:not(.eyebrow),
  .action-list p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75);
  }

  .action-section .section-intro .tool-note {
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .tool-note strong {
    color: #fff;
  }

  .action-list {
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.25);
  }

  .action-list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 28px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 18px;
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
  }

  .step-number {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding-top: 4px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1800px) {
    .method-header {
      min-height: 84px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .method-hero,
    .principles,
    .action-section,
    .question-grid,
    .response-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .position-note {
      max-width: 560px;
    }

    .question-grid,
    .response-grid {
      gap: 28px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 620px) {
    .method-wordmark > span:last-child {
      display: none;
    }

    .method-nav ol {
      column-gap: 16px;
    }

    .method-nav li {
      flex-basis: 120px;
    }

    .method-hero {
      padding-block: 56px;
    }
  }
</style>